      "page_title": "BRIN Opclasses, Partial and Expression Indexes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "PG 14 Opclasses"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Opclass",
            "What it fixes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`int8_minmax_multi_ops`",
              "several intervals per range"
            ],
            [
              "",
              "tolerates outliers"
            ],
            [
              "`int8_bloom_ops`",
              "per-range bloom filter"
            ],
            [
              "",
              "equality on uncorrelated data"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "CLUSTER Creates Correlation",
          "text": "`CLUSTER` on a btree index physically reorders the table, but it takes an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock and the table does not stay clustered."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "BRIN Refuses",
          "items": [
            "No sorting",
            "No uniqueness",
            "No index-only scans"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Partial Index",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at)",
            "WHERE status = 'pending';",
            "-- only pending rows enter the index"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Smaller index means faster scans",
            "Less write amplification on the table",
            "Excluded rows cost nothing on `INSERT` or `UPDATE`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Classic pattern: index the tiny hot slice of a huge table",
            "Unprocessed jobs waiting in a queue",
            "`soft_deleted = false` rows",
            "Active subscriptions among millions of dead ones"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Planner Must Prove It"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "index used",
                "lines": [
                  "`WHERE status = 'pending'`",
                  "literal repeats predicate",
                  "implication provable"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "index ignored",
                "lines": [
                  "`WHERE status = $1`",
                  "parameter, value unknown",
                  "proof is syntactic only"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep the index `WHERE` clause simple",
            "Repeat it literally in every query that should use it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON users (email)",
            "WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;",
            "-- one live email, many deleted ones"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cheapest Win Available",
          "items": [
            "`WHERE col IS NOT NULL` on a mostly-NULL column",
            "Shrinks the index by orders of magnitude",
            "Costs the queries nothing at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Expression Index"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX ON users (lower(email));",
            "WHERE lower(email) = lower($1)  -- used",
            "WHERE email = $1          -- never used"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "IMMUTABLE Or Nothing",
          "text": "Any function in an expression index must be IMMUTABLE. `now()`, `current_date` and unqualified `timestamptz` to `date` casts are not."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Expression",
            "Serves"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`date_trunc('day', ts)`",
              "daily buckets"
            ],
            [
              "`(data->>'user_id')`",
              "jsonb field lookup"
            ],
            [
              "`(col::text)`",
              "type-matched compare"
            ],
            [
              "`(a + b)`",
              "computed predicate"
            ],
            [
              "`md5(long_text)`",
              "long-key equality"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Expression Stats, Index-Only Scans, INCLUDE",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The planner collects separate statistics on the expression result",
            "Sometimes worth creating an index just for those estimates"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- partial and expression combine freely",
            "CREATE INDEX ON events ((payload->>'type'))",
            "WHERE created_at > '2026-01-01';"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "What You Pay, What Else Works",
          "items": [
            "The function runs on every insert and update of the row",
            "`citext` handles case-insensitive matching natively",
            "Or a generated column plus an ordinary index (PG 12+)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Skip The Heap",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An index-only scan returns every needed column from the index",
            "The heap is not touched at all",
            "Single biggest speedup available on wide tables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two Requirements",
          "items": [
            "Every column referenced anywhere is in the index",
            "That means `SELECT`, `WHERE`, `ORDER BY`, `GROUP BY`",
            "The heap page is marked all-visible in the visibility map",
            "Needed because index tuples carry no MVCC info"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Visibility Map"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "p0 vis+froz",
                "p1 vis"
              ],
              [
                "p2 dirty",
                "p3 vis+froz"
              ]
            ],
            "caption": "2 bits per heap page"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only `VACUUM` sets the bits",
            "Any write to the page clears them",
            "So a freshly written table still hits the heap",
            "Run `VACUUM`, or wait for autovacuum, then re-measure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Heap Fetches"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) SELECT id FROM t",
            "WHERE id BETWEEN 1 AND 100;",
            "-- Heap Fetches: 0   true index-only",
            "-- Heap Fetches: 100 stale visibility map"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "INCLUDE Columns"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX ON t (a) INCLUDE (b, c);",
            "-- b and c live in leaf pages only",
            "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON t (email)",
            "  INCLUDE (name);  -- unique on email"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "INCLUDE columns are not searchable and not sortable",
            "Keeping them out of the key keeps internal pages small",
            "They may be types btree cannot index at all",
            "A `UNIQUE` index covers extras without widening the constraint"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Covering Costs, Concurrent Builds, Index Health",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`count(*)` over a range can go index-only",
            "Which is why a narrow covering index beats a seq scan",
            "Dashboard counters are the obvious case"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Access method",
            "Index-only scan"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "btree",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "GiST",
              "some opclasses"
            ],
            [
              "SP-GiST",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "GIN, hash, BRIN",
              "never"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Do Not Cover Everything",
          "text": "A covering index is wider, so fewer entries fit per page: bigger index, slower writes. Never blindly INCLUDE every selected column."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two Habits",
          "items": [
            "Lower `autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor` on the hot table",
            "Keeps the visibility map fresh enough to stay index-only",
            "`SELECT *` guarantees a heap fetch, always",
            "List the columns you actually need"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Build Without Blocking",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY ON t (a);",
            "-- two table passes, no ACCESS EXCLUSIVE",
            "-- cannot run in a transaction block",
            "REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx;  -- PG 12+"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Bloat Is MVCC",
          "items": [
            "`UPDATE` writes a new row version",
            "Plus a new entry in every non-HOT-updated index",
            "A HOT update skips index maintenance entirely",
            "Needs unchanged indexed columns and room on the page"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Measuring Indexes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, idx_scan",
            "FROM pg_stat_user_indexes",
            "WHERE idx_scan = 0;  -- never used",
            "SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('i'));"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Check across a full business cycle before dropping anything",
            "Monthly jobs make an index look dead on a Tuesday",
            "`pgstattuple` or `pg_stat_user_indexes` estimate bloat",
            "`REINDEX CONCURRENTLY` rebuilds a bloated index online",
            "`DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY` removes one without blocking readers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When A Concurrent Build Fails"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT indexrelid::regclass FROM pg_index",
            "WHERE indisvalid = false;",
            "DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY bad_idx;",
            "-- then retry the build"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A failed concurrent build leaves an INVALID index behind",
            "It is never used by any query",
            "But it is still maintained on every write",
            "Drop it concurrently, then start the build again"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Maintenance, Mistakes, and Choosing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Killers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Query",
            "Why",
            "Repair"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`date(created_at) = d`",
              "function wraps column",
              "use a range"
            ],
            [
              "int col vs text param",
              "type mismatch",
              "cast the parameter"
            ],
            [
              "`LIKE '%foo'`",
              "leading wildcard",
              "pg_trgm GIN"
            ],
            [
              "index on a boolean",
              "low cardinality",
              "partial on rare value"
            ],
            [
              "`a = 1 OR b = 2`",
              "bitmap OR or seq scan",
              "UNION ALL"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`varchar` vs `text` under different collations disables it too",
            "Too many indexes on a write-heavy table hurts every row change",
            "Each one is a synchronous write plus WAL"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Stale Stats Beat Every Index",
          "text": "Run `ANALYZE` after bulk loads, and raise `default_statistics_target` (default 100) on skewed columns."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- index thrown away",
            "WHERE date(created_at) = '2026-01-01'",
            "-- index used",
            "WHERE created_at >= '2026-01-01'",
            "  AND created_at <  '2026-01-02'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same rows returned, one index scan instead of a seq scan",
            "The predicate moves from `Filter` to `Index Cond`",
            "`Rows Removed by Filter` falls to zero"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Foreign Keys Get No Index",
          "text": "`PRIMARY KEY` and `UNIQUE` create an index implicitly. `FOREIGN KEY` columns get none — a classic source of slow cascading deletes."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Retune For SSD",
          "items": [
            "Set `random_page_cost = 1.1` on SSD",
            "The 4.0 default assumes spinning disks",
            "It quietly suppresses index use everywhere"
          ]
        },
