  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of POSTGRES INDEXES. Most slow Postgres queries already have an index — it just is not the one the planner can use. This handbook opens up btree, hash, GIN, GiST and BRIN from the inside: page splits, posting lists, block summaries, visibility bits, and the exact reason `WHERE date(created_at) = ...` throws your index away. Ten pages, from the cost constants to the workflow that turns a Filter into an Index Cond.",
